# Embedding service configuration.
#
# Copy to .env in this folder to configure `docker compose up` run FROM HERE. Running the
# root stack instead reads the repo-root .env, not this one — Compose only picks up the
# .env next to the file it was invoked with. Same variable names either way.
#
# These are the COMPOSE-level names. docker-compose.yaml maps them to the unprefixed
# names the app reads (EMBEDDINGS_MODEL_ID -> MODEL_ID), so the prefix keeps them from
# colliding with the reranker's. Running uvicorn directly, without Compose, means setting
# the unprefixed names instead — see the right-hand column.

# --- Model ---
# Any sentence-transformers model. The default is MIT-licensed and 1024 dims.
#                                                                         (app: MODEL_ID)
# EMBEDDINGS_MODEL_ID=microsoft/harrier-oss-v1-0.6b

# "cpu", "cuda", or empty to let sentence-transformers decide.        (app: MODEL_DEVICE)
# EMBEDDINGS_DEVICE=cpu

# --- Throughput and limits ---
# Texts encoded per forward pass. Raise on a GPU, lower if memory is tight.
#                                                                  (app: MAX_BATCH_SIZE)
# EMBEDDINGS_BATCH_SIZE=32

# Inputs accepted in a single /v1/embeddings request.                   (app: MAX_INPUTS)
# EMBEDDINGS_MAX_INPUTS=256

# --- Instruction prefix ---
# Instruction-tuned models expect a prefix on QUERIES ONLY, never on documents; that is
# what the request's `task` field selects. Set false for models that use their own
# prefixes or none, such as BGE and E5.                            (app: USE_INSTRUCTION)
# EMBEDDINGS_USE_INSTRUCTION=true

# Overrides the built-in instruction. Leave unset to keep the default, which is tuned for
# retrieval; an empty value is treated as unset.                (app: DEFAULT_INSTRUCTION)
# EMBEDDINGS_INSTRUCTION=Given a web search query, retrieve relevant passages that answer the query

# --- Matryoshka ---
# Whether this model was trained with Matryoshka representation learning — i.e. whether a
# truncated vector is still a good vector. Only set true for models that document it.
#
# Declared rather than detected on purpose. Slicing any embedding works arithmetically and
# re-normalizing gives back a unit vector of the requested size, so a model without MRL
# training answers `dimensions` with something plausible whose retrieval quality has
# quietly collapsed. With this false the API returns 400 instead. The default model does
# not document MRL; Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B does, down to 32.       (app: SUPPORTS_MRL)
# EMBEDDINGS_SUPPORTS_MRL=false

# --- Access control ---
# Optional shared secret. When set, callers must send `Authorization: Bearer <key>`, and
# the backend must send the same value. Shared with the reranker on purpose: both are
# internal services behind the same trust boundary.               (app: INFERENCE_API_KEY)
# INFERENCE_API_KEY=

# --- Not configurable here ---
# HF_HOME is fixed to /models by the Dockerfile, because docker-compose.yaml mounts
# ./models there to cache the weights across restarts. Changing one without the other
# re-downloads the model on every start.
#
# The service listens on 8000 and publishes no host port: only the backend reaches it,
# over the compose network. Add a `ports:` entry to call it directly.
